{
  "id": "haman",
  "name": "Haman (son of Hammedatha)",
  "title": "The Malicious Advisor",
  "era": "exile",
  "lifespan": "c. 480–470 BC",
  "summary": "Haman was an Agagite and a high-ranking official at King Ahasuerus's court in Persia. He is known as the antagonist in the Book of Esther, where he planned to exterminate all Jews in the Persian Empire due to his personal hatred for the Jew Mordecai. His evil plans were exposed by Queen Esther, and he ended up being executed on the same gallows he had built for Mordecai.",
